[2861]={["atomIDs"]={"2861:description:1-135","2861:description:138-185","2861:description:190-225","2861:description:228-305","2861:description:310-397","2861:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="Ursyn had heard that Tabetha held a grievance against a Zul'Farrak troll. The mage in Dustwallow could explain it, though any resulting journey into the troll city promised danger.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with Tabetha at her Dustwallow cottage.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="002f54e7a8b7509bb9b9f669bfff3ccc088723c9e2dc0d7c5fc477cc5bbd5b77",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2862]={["atomIDs"]={"2862:description:1-13","2862:description:15-44","2862:description:47-108","2862:description:111-279","2862:description:284-354","2862:description:357-481","2862:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Hadoken saw the Woodpaw attacks growing more fevered around Camp Mojache. He feared the gnolls might drive the camp from Feralas and demanded ten manes as evidence of pressure on them.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather ten Woodpaw Gnoll Manes for Hadoken.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Woodpaw Gnoll Manes to Hadoken Swiftstrider.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b6b16636fd3d46dbc72affe802716053116dc5ad789c16ea53bae26e35b9e2cd",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2863]={["atomIDs"]={"2863:description:1-122","2863:description:125-242","2863:description:245-354","2863:description:359-501","2863:objective:1-73"},["bridge"]="The mane collection had returned to Hadoken. He now proposed striking five Woodpaw alphas within an hour, hoping a rapid loss of leaders would disrupt the coordinated attacks.",["bridgeFrom"]=2862,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Hadoken proposed a rapid strike at the Woodpaw leaders. Five alphas removed within one hour might spread chaos through their ranks and break the impasse around the camp.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake the timed assignment against five Woodpaw Alphas.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against five Woodpaw Alphas and returned to Hadoken within an hour.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="9dbb4f5c5646cd71b22266c437cd4712007a32434e870908f87ec88a52fb550b",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2864]={["atomIDs"]={"2864:description:1-38","2864:description:41-113","2864:description:116-206","2864:description:211-243","2864:description:246-324","2864:description:329-374","2864:objective:1-33"},["opening"]="Tran'rek's overdue scarab shells had strained Krazek's patience with his cousin. Before resorting to threats in person, he asked someone to visit Gadgetzan and press for the shipment.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Tran'rek about Krazek's delivery.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Tran'rek in Gadgetzan.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ec2e46c71ee99657993efb5f6128c32c08417a1d37ed460a717f7e6ae9f2d64d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2865]={["atomIDs"]={"2865:description:1-45","2865:description:48-108","2865:description:111-125","2865:description:130-167","2865:description:169-215","2865:description:220-334","2865:description:337-344","2865:description:349-392","2865:description:395-446","2865:description:451-462","2865:description:465-509","2865:objective:1-57"},["opening"]="Tran'rek valued scarab shells as building material, but overhunting had nearly exhausted their source. A colony within Zul'Farrak offered five uncracked shells for his delayed supply.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather five Uncracked Scarab Shells for Tran'rek.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five Uncracked Scarab Shells to Tran'rek.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="48b3ad9e8e15201cca0dfda54281b7ec21b70b12f53df8c72678f0ed0edc20cb",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2866]={["atomIDs"]={"2866:description:1-88","2866:description:91-178","2866:description:183-262","2866:description:265-322","2866:description:325-412","2866:description:417-490","2866:description:492-505","2866:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="The old Solarsal ruins had seemed unremarkable when the Sentinels first explored them. Now Hatecrest naga occupied them in alarming numbers, and Shandris suspected more than preparations for an attack.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to investigate the naga presence in the Ruins of Solarsal.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the investigation at the Ruins of Solarsal.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3c2aedc9fa2784f2ba96983aec1539f11c521980b0bc9e968c32573b72c411c5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2867]={["atomIDs"]={"2867:description:1-207","2867:objective:1-86"},["opening"]="A strange gazebo stood in the heart of Solarsal. Its discovery was the finding to be reported back across the island to General Shandris Feathermoon.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to report the gazebo discovery to Shandris.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the Solarsal findings to Shandris Feathermoon.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="1ebbf1495216f0d592970cda6bdfb9db2502226823da51dff0c194db8834f73b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2869]={["atomIDs"]={"2869:description:1-159","2869:description:162-239","2869:description:244-349","2869:description:352-508","2869:objective:1-81"},["opening"]="The naga's purpose remained uncertain, but Latronicus expected them eventually to claim the island. He called for action before that possibility hardened into control, requesting ten intact scales as proof.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover ten Hatecrest Naga Scales for Latronicus.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Hatecrest Naga Scales to Latronicus Moonspear.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="29eb2094d899e14c3efbad4ca19136e99439f2dfa11344a47ec52475153f0819",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2870]={["atomIDs"]={"2870:description:1-80","2870:description:83-173","2870:description:178-251","2870:description:254-415","2870:description:420-504","2870:objective:1-124"},["bridge"]="The scale assignment had reached Latronicus as scouts identified Lord Shalzaru's place in the naga command. The lord's excavated relic on the Isle of Dread became the next object of both attack and study.",["bridgeFrom"]=2869,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Scouts identified Lord Shalzaru among the naga royals directing the occupation. He had reportedly uncovered a relic in a cave on the Isle of Dread; Latronicus wanted both the leader stopped and his find brought back for study.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Lord Shalzaru and recover the Mysterious Relic.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Shalzaru assignment and delivered the Mysterious Relic to Latronicus.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3ba94cd6cb879f44bf9041b2c56f96317b98201f3b2ff1e5524372647765c73e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2871]={["aftermath"]="Vestia's first impression placed the relic outside both Solarsal's native craft and naga design. Its alien character required further research rather than an immediate identification.",["atomIDs"]={"2871:description:1-89","2871:description:92-211","2871:description:214-294","2871:description:297-369","2871:description:371-390","2871:description:395-440","2871:description:443-453","2871:objective:1-75"},["bridge"]="The Mysterious Relic had reached Latronicus, whose military knowledge could not explain it. Vestia's scholarship and priestly learning offered the next avenue of inquiry.",["bridgeFrom"]=2870,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2871:completion:1-14","2871:completion:16-61","2871:completion:64-111","2871:completion:114-167","2871:completion:170-209","2871:completion:211-241","2871:completion:246-297","2871:completion:300-391","2871:completion:396-475"},["opening"]="Latronicus could not explain the recovered device. His wife Vestia combined priestly service with scholarship, making her the person he trusted to discover what the relic was.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver the Mysterious Relic to Vestia.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Mysterious Relic to Vestia Moonspear.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6fa45fc886dcf9077a711bc12dd8b3fb25b93cc29df3de8fa49d268837fca26c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2872]={["atomIDs"]={"2872:description:1-57","2872:description:60-209","2872:description:212-325","2872:description:330-435","2872:description:438-510","2872:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="MacKinley's old friend Stoley had wagered that Steamwheedle rum surpassed Booty Bay's. The promised bottle had not arrived, and Sea Wolf wanted the barman visited before the debt escaped him.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with Stoley about the rum wager.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Stoley in Steamwheedle Port.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="25fda00f3ebe17a04f8694d321acab2a8c0f5d2f306e1215a6ee3df6c416793d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2873]={["atomIDs"]={"2873:description:1-90","2873:description:93-192","2873:description:197-336","2873:objective:1-55"},["bridge"]="The wager inquiry had reached Stoley. His promised rum was missing because Cuergo stole the shipment and stored it in the walled pirate town south of the port.",["bridgeFrom"]=2872,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Stoley could not settle his wager because Cuergo had stolen the last rum shipment. The bottles were stored in the walled pirate town to the south, where recovery could supply his promised proof of Kalimdor's liquor.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Stoley's Shipment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned Stoley's Shipment to him at Steamwheedle Port.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="f1fe1d1def302bc5d4e24a6492a472581308d04b92958ac26863010e0800848b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2874]={["aftermath"]="MacKinley found the rum harsh enough to satisfy Stoley's claim and allowed his friend to keep the wagered money. The long delivery settled a personal bet.",["atomIDs"]={"2874:description:1-31","2874:description:34-75","2874:description:78-169","2874:objective:1-59"},["bridge"]="The rum shipment had been recovered. Stoley sent one bottle back to MacKinley, ready to let its strength settle their argument.",["bridgeFrom"]=2873,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2874:completion:1-21","2874:completion:26-44","2874:completion:46-61","2874:completion:63-71","2874:completion:73-85","2874:completion:90-139","2874:completion:141-191","2874:completion:193-245"},["opening"]="The recovered supply had yielded a bottle of Steamwheedle bilge rum for MacKinley. Stoley sent it back to Booty Bay to settle their dispute over the better drink.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to deliver Stoley's Bottle to MacKinley.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Stoley's Bottle to Sea Wolf MacKinley.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="9f93f5270c90ac740465e266b5bcc018285741189f2a41c528a885b676e218b0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2875]={["atomIDs"]={"2875:description:1-88","2875:description:93-234","2875:description:239-475","2875:objective:1-71"},["opening"]="Andre Firebeard was wanted for crimes against Steamwheedle and Gadgetzan. The notice authorized lethal force and allowed his head to stand as proof before the port's security chief.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring Andre's Head to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Andre's Head to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="d92d5d88ddd21489a7c4ec8113832cc240a99d8a47eac2c1af06908432fbc66d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2876]={["aftermath"]="The security chief recognized the schedules' accuracy and the danger of pirates possessing them. His reply treated the document as evidence of an exposed shipping route.",["atomIDs"]={"2876:description:1-88","2876:description:90-269","2876:description:274-334","2876:objective:1-63"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2876:completion:1-109","2876:completion:112-200","2876:completion:205-239","2876:completion:242-271","2876:completion:276-289","2876:completion:292-371"},["opening"]="A scroll listed past and future shipments between the two goblin ports. Marks beside selected voyages and notes about loot and resistance made its schedules evidence for Steamwheedle's authorities.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to report the Ship Schedules at Steamwheedle Port.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the Ship Schedules to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="83bda3e11d6154ce882b81aea5ea0d2d8766f167680609f1f385bb49cd37af25",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2877]={["aftermath"]="Fraggar described the effort as preparation for extending Wildhammer influence.",["atomIDs"]={"2877:description:1-70","2877:description:73-143","2877:description:148-267","2877:description:270-355","2877:description:360-394","2877:description:397-491","2877:description:494-502","2877:objective:1-101"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2877:completion:1-46","2877:completion:49-113","2877:completion:118-197","2877:completion:200-305","2877:completion:307-395"},["opening"]="Fraggar wanted deeds before friendship. The abandoned positions near Skulk Rock had become ooze-infested, obstructing Wildhammer plans for a wider presence there.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to confront ten sludges and ten oozes.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Fraggar's cleanup assignment.",["sourceHash"]="d7a0502d1f6a03d888b925aecd34bef841dc6c584302190a14f7e5e527aeed56",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2879]={["aftermath"]="The energized stave opened a small door in the monolith, exposing the artifact within as light filled the surrounding space.",["atomIDs"]={"2879:description:1-41","2879:description:43-185","2879:description:190-276","2879:description:278-388","2879:description:390-508","2879:objective:1-53"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2879:completion:1-49","2879:completion:51-86","2879:completion:91-150","2879:completion:155-228","2879:completion:233-289"},["opening"]="Troyas suspected the stave was the key to Equinex Monolith. Four flames in Ravenwind held the essences needed to energize it; only then could its identity and the artifact within the monolith be tested.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather the four flame essences, energize Troyas' Stave and find Equinex Monolith.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the stave-energizing and Equinex Monolith assignment.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b4475e5fbbb1c9a4f6bf2acb293c64c1ea078b367ff7fc7f53f946fa7aa0e530",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2880]={["aftermath"]="Fraggar accepted the act as a step toward Wildhammer friendship.",["atomIDs"]={"2880:description:1-56","2880:description:59-235","2880:description:240-309","2880:description:312-404","2880:description:407-496","2880:objective:1-70"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2880:completion:1-35","2880:completion:38-109","2880:completion:112-164","2880:completion:169-223"},["opening"]="Fraggar emphasized the Wildhammers' independence from the Alliance in this account. Five tribal necklaces would serve as a concrete demonstration of willingness to work for their favor.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring five necklaces to Fraggar.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the necklaces at Aerie Peak.",["sourceHash"]="13b6f8932921b7ec5847a3bf91115bcad957449266fd38a24fdf12b87e4ce2b3",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2882]={["atomIDs"]={"2882:description:1-55","2882:description:58-102","2882:description:109-124","2882:description:127-139","2882:description:142-171","2882:description:174-202","2882:description:205-232","2882:description:235-272","2882:description:275-309","2882:objective:1-19"},["opening"]="A treasure map pointed to a southern beach below Wheedle. Its mast, flag, and bones marked Cuergo's buried gold, but the directions also warned of a key and men ready to fight.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to follow the map and find Cuergo's gold.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for Cuergo's gold.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="2dfc21cd2a4d183b15addd101bb607ccbb626d7e7600a67a8ae380b81e45c8e9",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2902]={["atomIDs"]={"2902:description:1-132","2902:description:135-232","2902:description:237-332","2902:description:335-427","2902:description:430-476","2902:objective:1-86"},["opening"]="The Woodpaw attacks seemed too coordinated for Hadoken to regard them as impulse. He wanted battle plans from the southern camps to explain the gnolls' recent behavior.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the Woodpaw camps for battle plans.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for the gnoll battle plans.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e6c4df369e36d54af5ea92530dd86c05428750d2b95cf1179569d2ccaec08698",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2903]={["atomIDs"]={"2903:description:1-136","2903:description:139-218","2903:objective:1-71"},["bridge"]="The search of the camps had yielded Woodpaw Battle Plans. Their discovery still needed to become knowledge at Camp Mojache through delivery to Hadoken.",["bridgeFrom"]=2902,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The Woodpaw plans had been discovered. They needed to reach Hadoken at Camp Mojache before anyone there could judge what lay behind the attacks.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the Woodpaw Battle Plans to Hadoken.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Woodpaw Battle Plans to Hadoken Swiftstrider.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="d84e42c51371aafd2eda61b96a9d6c6a71f8faa0e95e5a9a4313c171172411d2",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2904]={["atomIDs"]={"2904:description:1-24","2904:description:26-39","2904:description:44-205","2904:description:210-232","2904:description:237-443","2904:description:448-463","2904:objective:1-81"},["opening"]="Kernobee recalled Dark Iron dwarves beating him and throwing him among troggs. He wanted help reaching the exit, then word sent to Scooty while he went to warn Tinkerwiz about their involvement in the rig.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to escort Kernobee to Clockwerk Run and report to Scooty.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Kernobee's escort to the Clockwerk Run exit and reported to Scooty.",["sourceHash"]="8d174dca78348f80cb6c2e060a31921bca1d6feb8fee9b692fdcafc2818cc9f8",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2922]={["aftermath"]="Overspark prepared to begin work on the recovered core. He hoped to repair Techbot, but the return of the component did not itself establish that the machine was fixed.",["atomIDs"]={"2922:description:1-96","2922:description:99-234","2922:description:237-258","2922:description:260-296","2922:description:299-330","2922:description:335-365","2922:description:368-507","2922:objective:1-65"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2922:completion:1-22","2922:completion:25-38","2922:completion:41-70","2922:completion:75-95","2922:completion:97-111","2922:completion:114-133","2922:completion:138-203"},["opening"]="Overspark believed Gnomeregan's fall had reversed Techbot's behavior through a polarized brain. The once-helpful machine now roamed in a frenzy, but its memory core might still reveal a way to repair it.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Techbot's Memory Core for Overspark.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Techbot's Memory Core to Tinkmaster Overspark.",["sourceHash"]="c8a89eb94af4db8739b07b2ed842092a7287cc2e83873399d2a8d54e5bd40a05",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2923]={["atomIDs"]={"2923:description:1-85","2923:description:88-191","2923:description:196-204","2923:description:207-244","2923:description:249-309","2923:description:312-338","2923:objective:1-45"},["opening"]="Sarno remembered Techbot as a helpful machine and regretted hearing of its malfunction. He directed possible help to its distressed creator, Tinkmaster Overspark, in Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Tinkmaster Overspark about Techbot.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="3fec1c0168359ef58564961563d399a37eb332d638711549de81a19a956304e8",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2924]={["atomIDs"]={"2924:description:1-122","2924:description:125-226","2924:description:229-293","2924:description:298-362","2924:description:365-465","2924:description:470-501","2924:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Gnomeregan's hurried evacuation had left essential artificials behind. Klockmort needed a dozen of the versatile components for new work, stored in extrapolator containers deep in the abandoned city.",["pending"]="{actor} would retrieve twelve Essential Artificials for Klockmort.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twelve Essential Artificials to Klockmort Spannerspan.",["sourceHash"]="b4a8ec9c4b65be2e3b7f6e0aecfd555516d3c2c3b3a0aad4206a189ccf286097",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2925]={["atomIDs"]={"2925:description:1-70","2925:description:73-242","2925:description:247-301","2925:description:304-367","2925:description:372-422","2925:objective:1-46"},["opening"]="Mathiel had received a request from his friend Klockmort for help entering contaminated Gnomeregan. Unable to leave his own work, he asked another to go to Ironforge in his place.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to meet Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="56aec34691d31a7ad1174b1ff3004d98813cf6dad8ee150d618bdd1f9234e8aa",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2926]={["atomIDs"]={"2926:description:1-164","2926:description:169-275","2926:description:277-304","2926:description:306-436","2926:description:438-494","2926:objective:1-116","2926:objective:118-179"},["bridge"]="Ozzie's proposal needed material from the very sickness it sought to treat. Fallout drawn from Gnomeregan's irradiated troggs would supply the first sample. Until it was tested, even the inventors could not say whether they were approaching a cure or something closer to potent rum.",["bridgeFrom"]=2927,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Ozzie and Razzle thought their experiments might lead toward a cure for Gnomeregan's sickness, though testing remained essential. Fallout from irradiated troggs was the next material needed to distinguish hope from a failed concoction.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to fill the Leaden Collection Phial with radioactive fallout for Ozzie.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned with a phial of the troggs' green glow.",["sourceHash"]="0abd98d52add0a7cec943974f9830aa4653f75c22c53cb97f8ffd54319b181f0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2927]={["atomIDs"]={"2927:description:1-42","2927:description:44-60","2927:description:62-135","2927:description:137-195","2927:description:200-235","2927:description:240-287","2927:description:292-321","2927:description:323-372","2927:description:374-411","2927:description:413-464","2927:objective:1-40"},["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Radiation had taken Gnoarn's remarkable hair when Gnomeregan fell into disaster. His anger fixed on the troggs, but saving the city would take more than curses. In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle were working on a remedy.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} carried Gnoarn's appeal to Ozzie in Kharanos.",["sourceHash"]="4c26d2a0d5365e5e27429f907691de4bb821661cd457b62bdcc4e2b1157a16d1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2928]={["atomIDs"]={"2928:description:1-18","2928:description:20-122","2928:description:127-159","2928:description:161-234","2928:description:236-314","2928:description:319-388","2928:description:390-420","2928:description:422-452","2928:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="A shortage of parts threatened Shoni's effort to send excavation machines to Dun Morogh. Gnomeregan's roaming robots offered a source of salvage, and she called for two dozen sets of their mechanical workings.",["pending"]="{actor} would gather twenty-four Robo-mechanical Guts for Shoni.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twenty-four Robo-mechanical Guts to Shoni in Stormwind.",["sourceHash"]="ff00412e99859cb324ed6fc5b1fe209ac834870e8864b3dc713aa8f9ad023c73",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2929]={["aftermath"]="Mekkatorque counted Thermaplugg's death as a step toward reclaiming Gnomeregan. The city itself had not been restored by the assignment.",["atomIDs"]={"2929:description:1-26","2929:description:28-100","2929:description:102-114","2929:description:116-121","2929:description:123-129","2929:description:131-172","2929:description:174-243","2929:description:245-267","2929:description:272-301","2929:description:303-357","2929:description:359-438","2929:description:440-469","2929:objective:1-53","2929:objective:55-114"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2929:completion:1-111","2929:completion:113-208"},["opening"]="Mekkatorque condemned Thermaplugg's betrayal of the gnomish people and the loss of their home. He sought the usurper's death as part of the continuing struggle to retake Gnomeregan.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to confront Mekgineer Thermaplugg and report to Mekkatorque.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Mekgineer Thermaplugg and returned to High Tinker Mekkatorque.",["sourceHash"]="25be94f2a0c5037f02dc52b2adb116292f6fa54bb1cae3818f14d4229bd1a786",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2930]={["atomIDs"]={"2930:description:1-53","2930:description:56-78","2930:description:83-201","2930:description:204-275","2930:description:277-356","2930:description:359-426","2930:description:428-471","2930:description:476-494","2930:description:497-509","2930:objective:1-70"},["opening"]="Castpipe needed data left behind in Gnomeregan. The highest-security Punchograph terminal required clearance earned through lower terminals, beginning with a white card and ending with the prismatic card he sought.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover a Prismatic Punch Card for Castpipe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered a Prismatic Punch Card to Master Mechanic Castpipe.",["sourceHash"]="83bcb14d5ad55c9b1b73cb7c1257c7b0bffbb25df4bbbe448ace056d0ad3f22f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2931]={["atomIDs"]={"2931:description:1-62","2931:description:65-167","2931:description:172-445","2931:description:450-469","2931:objective:1-49"},["opening"]="Gaxim passed on Castpipe's call for a high-security data retrieval mission into Gnomeregan. He trusted the mechanic's judgment enough to direct recruits to Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to consult Master Mechanic Castpipe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="a562395c46ff53540e76cd713e1881fc006f20bb2a86c36b70f994bf9c176946",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2932]={["aftermath"]="News had reached Nimboya, who hoped the Witherbark would heed the warning.",["atomIDs"]={"2932:description:1-80","2932:description:82-107","2932:description:112-174","2932:description:177-262","2932:description:267-321","2932:description:324-435","2932:description:440-487","2932:objective:1-53","2932:objective:56-176"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2932:completion:1-29","2932:completion:31-60","2932:completion:62-107"},["opening"]="Nimboya accused the Witherbark of betraying Thrall. His pike was to bear skulls in one of their villages as a threat of consequences for that betrayal.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to plant the laden pike in a Witherbark village.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the display and returned to Nimboya.",["sourceHash"]="5d490ece2874daa5695e490b32a6eed33cfccdf95b4b15c8e901905052095a0c",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2933]={["aftermath"]="Lydon tentatively attributed the venom to an arachnoid source.",["atomIDs"]={"2933:description:1-39","2933:description:44-138","2933:description:141-204","2933:objective:1-53"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2933:completion:1-21","2933:completion:23-47","2933:completion:49-84","2933:completion:86-110"},["opening"]="The village held many bottles of green venom, suggesting unusual importance. A sample could place the substance before an apothecary in nearby Tarren Mill.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take a bottle to an apothecary.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the venom to Lydon.",["sourceHash"]="70dc6a74a9ad25760784a309f069f1f0dd5e6534c1bcc7e9e09ad731e80c47bc",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2934]={["atomIDs"]={"2934:description:1-55","2934:description:58-196","2934:description:199-260","2934:description:265-334","2934:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="Lydon needed the venom fresh from its source rather than stored in a bottle. Spiders near Shadra'Alor offered the first place to seek an undamaged sac.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver a fresh venom sac.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the intact sac to Lydon.",["sourceHash"]="c36531929e2aa4b23ef42b1079b707fccb2db47f919bfce8ce8da85f52c8db46",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2935]={["aftermath"]="Gadrin recognized the inquiry and warned that the explanation would be unwelcome.",["atomIDs"]={"2935:description:1-84","2935:description:87-128","2935:description:133-168","2935:description:171-296","2935:description:299-338","2935:description:341-400","2935:objective:1-44"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2935:completion:1-68","2935:completion:70-86","2935:completion:88-136"},["opening"]="The broodguards' venom proved weaker than the bottled sample. Lydon turned toward Gadrin's knowledge of the Witherbark to identify a different spider behind it.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to ask Gadrin about the stronger venom.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Gadrin in Sen'jin.",["sourceHash"]="b1257f8dc80ef6c419487078ee357e2001d2e51dc5cc1afca70169843861100a",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2936]={["aftermath"]="Gadrin recognized the name Elortha no Shadra and prepared to put it into a summoning spell. The learned name enabled a later rite rather than performing it at this meeting.",["atomIDs"]={"2936:description:1-88","2936:description:91-147","2936:description:152-311","2936:description:316-391","2936:description:394-424","2936:objective:1-107"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2936:completion:1-24","2936:completion:26-125","2936:completion:130-198"},["opening"]="Gadrin said the Witherbarks' strongest venom came from their spider god. Her true name was needed for a summoning, preserved on a tablet in Zul'Farrak's tomb guarded by Theka.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to read the Tablet of Theka and return with the spider god's name.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the tablet-reading assignment and returned to Master Gadrin.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="674a8d6256bba1697cd5e13a1cc855bcfeb531e05371b2769c43714f859192d7",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2937]={["atomIDs"]={"2937:description:1-113","2937:description:116-154","2937:objective:1-99"},["opening"]="Gadrin supplied words for the altar deep within Witherbark territory. Reading them would summon the spider god whose venom Lydon sought.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to summon Shadra and recover her venom.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Shadra's venom to Lydon.",["sourceHash"]="5c3ecbd8e9ec993290e4508aaa66817f04e01ca2387574e7149eb8cadf204d96",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2938]={["aftermath"]="Faranell welcomed the potent poison and hoped the Society would find further applications.",["atomIDs"]={"2938:description:1-72","2938:description:75-152","2938:description:155-354","2938:description:359-454","2938:description:457-505","2938:objective:1-71"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2938:completion:1-14","2938:completion:16-153","2938:completion:158-186","2938:completion:191-204","2938:completion:206-264"},["opening"]="Lydon reported startling potency in the new sample, while admitting some test rabbits were small and young. He sent a portion to his superior for independent experimentation.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take the parcel to Faranell.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Lydon's sample to the Undercity.",["sourceHash"]="31c8390327443c646c1856aeca8b382ec962f72ef3beebd2c1fd0aa0f6ece609",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2939]={["atomIDs"]={"2939:description:1-100","2939:description:105-209","2939:description:211-285","2939:description:287-373","2939:description:378-454","2939:description:456-511","2939:objective:1-46"},["opening"]="Troyas had found an ordinary-looking stave among Feralas' ruins but could not dismiss the sense that it meant more. His and Angelas' books gave no answer, so he turned to Daryn Lightwind for knowledge beyond their shelves.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to consult Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b571635fef514c7c06d4e5f16b1db970b34c8ba5de2210f17a4a77cb6293bb98",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2940]={["aftermath"]="Daryn agreed in principle to lend the book, attaching a favor before the loan could proceed.",["atomIDs"]={"2940:description:1-65","2940:description:67-201","2940:description:206-277","2940:objective:1-47"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2940:completion:1-44","2940:completion:49-63","2940:completion:68-151"},["opening"]="A worn, yellow-paged book appeared to answer Troyas' inquiry. Long unopened though it seemed, it still belonged to Daryn, whose permission was needed before borrowing it.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to ask Daryn for permission to borrow the book.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} asked Daryn Lightwind about borrowing her book.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="da99d237fbed9e44bed6a31e4e912003f99bb0ffe0831b2ce641801582ff19b1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2941]={["atomIDs"]={"2941:description:1-128","2941:description:130-204","2941:description:206-258","2941:description:260-313","2941:description:318-366","2941:description:368-430","2941:description:432-469","2941:objective:1-48"},["opening"]="Daryn's own research concerned Hinterlands snapjaws, especially the giant Gammerita. Unable to leave her work, she wanted a picture and sent a letter to Curgle, whose invention could capture one.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take Daryn's letter to Curgle Cranklehop.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Daryn's letter to Curgle Cranklehop in Tanaris.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3442d36f1299bd901d4ee95bf2fb8d9c9324895fbf8e85ba4afc5b35b9a5ac58",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2942]={["aftermath"]="Troyas identified the artifact as the Morrow Stone. He considered its concealment significant but remained uncertain of its purpose, leaving study still to come.",["atomIDs"]={"2942:description:1-112","2942:objective:1-99"},["bridge"]="The monolith had opened, but the stave's energy faded as its artifact was removed. The Sparkling Stone and Stave of Equinex were now bound back to Troyas together.",["bridgeFrom"]=2879,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2942:completion:1-39","2942:completion:41-93","2942:completion:95-268","2942:completion:273-360","2942:completion:362-389"},["opening"]="Removing the artifact from Equinex Monolith left the stave's power fading. The recovered Sparkling Stone and its key now needed to return together to Troyas at Feathermoon.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Sparkling Stone and Stave of Equinex to Troyas.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Sparkling Stone and Stave of Equinex to Troyas Moonbreeze.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a842f80e33b1ed840ccd088f154843b67147ee4cd1a54f75bfa2b567d1024308",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2943]={["atomIDs"]={"2943:description:1-15","2943:description:17-45","2943:description:50-66","2943:description:68-108","2943:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="Daryn entrusted her book to the waiting messenger, asking that it be handled carefully. Troyas' inquiry in Feralas was ready to receive the volume he needed.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to deliver Daryn's book to Troyas.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the book to Troyas Moonbreeze.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="590f358caaab376004522f105423e48505beca40c682393933f895f67443fab9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2944]={["atomIDs"]={"2944:description:1-44","2944:description:46-142","2944:description:147-209","2944:description:211-220","2944:description:222-249","2944:description:251-323","2944:description:328-365","2944:description:367-375","2944:objective:1-111"},["opening"]="Curgle's Super Snapper could fix a view with a target and a button. Gammerita remained to be found in the Hinterlands before Daryn could receive the picture she wanted for her study.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to photograph Gammerita with the Super Snapper FX and return to Daryn.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Gammerita snapshot assignment and returned to Daryn Lightwind.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ce6b5e1c8ae8f74d701353d88fd3652fec90ae90d85907d2541b21480741f6a1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2945]={["atomIDs"]={"2945:description:1-93","2945:description:96-234","2945:description:237-351","2945:description:356-476","2945:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="A ring taken from a Dark Iron corpse remained sealed under hardened grime. Hints of metal and a gem suggested value beneath the residue, but cleaning had to come before any use.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find a way to clean the Grime-Encrusted Ring.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment to remove the ring's grime.",["sourceHash"]="057fd1b0fb1f8822bdfc965cd562ce44209b99c7133b4b65c3a735095eea3fa5",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2946]={["aftermath"]="The discs reacted at the pedestal and a Stone Watcher appeared. It identified the missing Plates of Uldum as the condition of access, leaving the gates closed.",["atomIDs"]={"2946:description:1-79","2946:description:88-136","2946:description:141-185","2946:description:188-217","2946:description:220-264","2946:description:267-334","2946:description:337-397","2946:description:402-457","2946:description:460-504","2946:objective:1-124"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2946:completion:1-90","2946:completion:92-226","2946:completion:231-243","2946:completion:245-269","2946:completion:271-368","2946:completion:370-459","2946:completion:461-471"},["opening"]="Karnik did not know what the miniature discs would do at Uldum's sealed gates. A reaction, a hidden mechanism or even silence remained possible, making the desert visit an experiment.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the miniature discs to Uldum and investigate their connection.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the disc investigation at Uldum's gates.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="2e62aa57ddb4607d8aac3f2846b72daf0466b1228f71741aa83fa616daa5c4d7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2947]={["atomIDs"]={"2947:description:1-96","2947:description:99-160","2947:description:165-252","2947:description:255-309","2947:description:312-417","2947:description:420-435","2947:description:437-464","2947:description:467-489","2947:objective:1-126"},["opening"]="The cleaned ring bore Ironforge's seal and the initials TdK. The marks could name either its maker or former owner, leaving its holder a choice between keeping the ring and seeking that person.",["pending"]="{actor} would seek the person identified by the Ironforge ring's marks.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the cleaned ring to Talvash del Kissel.",["sourceHash"]="2518c61129494c5891263c0f9e722753d9c39505b31473772aa4b081483e4c8f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2948]={["atomIDs"]={"2948:description:1-38","2948:description:40-71","2948:description:74-116","2948:description:119-217","2948:description:220-263","2948:description:268-336","2948:description:339-476","2948:description:481-489","2948:objective:1-114"},["opening"]="Talvash considered his old ring design simple beside his present skill. A silver-and-agate lattice could improve it, but depleted stocks left the owner supplying materials as well as the fee.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Brilliant Gold Ring, Silver Bar, Moss Agate and thirty silver to Talvash.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Talvash's ring, material and thirty-silver turn-in.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="0c30f7cc9e846e0567df24d91a16abcd8cd7a8e48aa3247c4121a980e9995658",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2949]={["atomIDs"]={"2949:description:1-71","2949:description:74-136","2949:description:141-228","2949:description:231-327","2949:description:332-437","2949:description:440-455","2949:description:457-495","2949:objective:1-126"},["opening"]="Orgrimmar's seal and the letters NOG remained visible inside the cleaned ring. The inscription might identify a maker or previous owner, offering a lead if its holder chose to return it.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find the person indicated by the Orgrimmar ring's inscription.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the cleaned ring to Nogg.",["sourceHash"]="e910286af4cb21c3da59a9a5ce96d7e8de83cf4c22e2e6d2f333107ca40abf48",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2950]={["aftermath"]="Nogg returned the improved ring and continued considering the Dark Iron information a useful lead.",["atomIDs"]={"2950:description:1-68","2950:description:71-154","2950:description:157-260","2950:description:263-284","2950:description:289-467","2950:description:470-480","2950:objective:1-100"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2950:completion:1-37","2950:completion:40-102","2950:completion:105-211"},["opening"]="Nogg denied claiming ownership of the ring and instead offered improvement for useful intelligence. Silver, agate and a fee would strengthen its magic through a new lattice.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to supply the ring, metal, gem and fee.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the ring-improvement exchange.",["sourceHash"]="6d0e90449c14422e98e72e4d83b3785c2c36a63af00e2d483c7fcca1cc6183ec",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2951]={["atomIDs"]={"2951:description:1-96","2951:description:99-180","2951:description:185-226","2951:description:229-286","2951:description:289-370","2951:description:373-433","2951:description:436-479","2951:objective:1-118"},["opening"]="Among the gnomes holding out inside Gnomeregan stood a cleaning machine with a simple price. The Sparklematic's plaque promised to strip grime from an inserted item for three silver coins.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to place a Grime-Encrusted Item and three silver in the Sparklematic.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Sparklematic submission with a Grime-Encrusted Item and three silver.",["sourceHash"]="948aa2b3d9961e4794ad0b9c62d3db8812a44a645f0baefd40af4e989258d79b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2952]={["aftermath"]="The Sparklematic halted with a chime and opened to reveal a small wrapped box. Its packaging was clear; whether the machine had actually cleaned the object remained to be discovered.",["atomIDs"]={"2952:completion:1-72","2952:completion:74-160","2952:completion:162-229","2952:completion:231-321","2952:completion:323-404","2952:completion:409-475"},["availabilityQualification"]={["basis"]="Catalog states positive beta server experience; confirms reported definition, not that a player can reach its giver in the target release",["currentServerPlayableConfirmed"]=false,["eligibility"]="BETA_SERVER_DEFINED_PUBLISHER_CLAIM",["sourceReceipt"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639 ; https://tierhall.app/wow/quests/2952"},["completionOnly"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2952:completion:1-72","2952:completion:74-160","2952:completion:162-229","2952:completion:231-321","2952:completion:323-404","2952:completion:409-475"},["factSourceMetadata"]={["finisherIDs"]={},["finisherName"]=nil,["giverIDs"]={},["giverName"]=nil},["fieldBlockers"]={"Acceptance description absent.","Acceptance objective absent.","Opening, pending intention, and personal objective discharge remain source-blocked."},["kind"]="COMPLETION_ONLY",["minimumStage"]=4,["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="595a18077d0d6c00cd0cad2da0aff06916bbd6639add381f363263c10731518d",["sourceMapID"]="1426",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2953]={["atomIDs"]={"2953:requestItems:1-107"},["coverageQualification"]="BASIC_PROGRESS_EXCHANGE_CONTEXT",["minimumStage"]=3,["objectiveSummary"]="Give the Sparklematic a grime-encrusted object and three silver coins.",["opening"]="The Sparklematic stood ready to clean another grime-encrusted object. Three silver coins would start the machine; the nature of anything recovered depended on what was put inside.",["pending"]="{actor} would feed the object and three silver coins into the Sparklematic.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} paid three silver to have a grime-encrusted object cleaned.",["reviewStatus"]="RETAINED_PROGRESS_SOURCE_MARKERS_REVIEWED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_CERTIFIED",["sourceHash"]="0d377d1ee175e1323c9694ddc9b1d80ee23e4fecaa060e74c1d9c06662ee21fc",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639",["unresolvedFields"]={"currentPlayability","unrecordedPersonalOutcome"}},
[2954]={["aftermath"]="The Watcher repeated the condition for entry: the Plates of Uldum still had to be obtained and integrated. Learning its purpose did not grant access to the complex.",["atomIDs"]={"2954:description:1-40","2954:description:43-169","2954:description:174-327","2954:description:330-434","2954:objective:1-117"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2954:completion:1-61","2954:completion:66-130","2954:completion:132-257"},["opening"]="The Stone Watcher barred Uldum without the Plates integrated into the disc set. Its appearance answered the desert expedition's immediate question, but its purpose still had to be learned before using the pedestal.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to learn the Watcher's purpose and interact with the Uldum Pedestal.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Stone Watcher inquiry and Uldum Pedestal interaction.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4ba7316dae351f76d5287bf119cc6705f48f776a8d34cb5ca8022d849ff65c74",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2962]={["aftermath"]="Ozzie checked that the courier still had every limb, then prepared to see what the sample could do.",["atomIDs"]={"2962:description:1-70","2962:description:75-109","2962:description:111-184","2962:description:186-284","2962:description:286-345","2962:description:347-410","2962:description:412-503","2962:objective:1-69","2962:objective:71-138","2962:objective:143-227"},["bridge"]="Ozzie found the earlier material too weak and impure. He now wanted fallout from irradiated slimes, lurkers and horrors inside Gnomeregan. The stronger substance was harder to contain, turning the return to Kharanos into a race against its instability.",["bridgeFrom"]=2926,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["endingAtomIDs"]={"2962:completion:1-67","2962:completion:69-112"},["independentReviewRevision"]="r2-findings-applied-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Ozzie found the earlier sample too weak and impure. He now wanted fallout from Gnomeregan's irradiated slimes, lurkers or horrors, warning that both collection and the unstable sample itself could fail.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring High Potency Radioactive Fallout and the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial to Ozzie.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="The stronger fallout reached Ozzie in the heavy collection phial {actor} carried.",["sourceHash"]="c598c2308c1108357b708900b47ef3b39689bbfcfbfa59a75a2c0aa07579cfff",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2963]={["atomIDs"]={"2963:description:1-25","2963:description:28-109","2963:description:112-203","2963:description:206-317","2963:description:322-448","2963:description:451-502","2963:objective:1-70"},["opening"]="The discoveries in Uldaman had set the League studying the miniature discs. Karnik's clues about Tanaris's Valley of the Watchers were ready for a conversation in the Hall of Explorers.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Historian Karnik about Uldum.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Historian Karnik in Ironforge.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3539470caf06471dd7c553b193c9ec0e6ba9e113a4cabd72629429d873ed3670",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2964]={["aftermath"]="Magellas agreed to suspend fieldwork until research narrowed the Plates' location. The investigation had an honest temporary end, not an opened Uldum.",["atomIDs"]={"2964:description:1-10","2964:description:12-54","2964:description:57-141","2964:description:144-231","2964:description:234-357","2964:description:362-494","2964:objective:1-47"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2964:completion:1-149","2964:completion:152-269","2964:completion:274-423","2964:completion:426-462","2964:completion:464-477"},["opening"]="The researchers knew they needed the Plates of Uldum but not where to find them. Karnik called the impasse temporary and sent the current state of the investigation back to Magellas.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to inform High Explorer Magellas of the research impasse.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with High Explorer Magellas.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e0b60ac431b5e22bf5d1f60ea3876d7e3ebc1d09d580f45ab239d471e872aa99",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2965]={["aftermath"]="She distinguished seeing Uldum's exterior from entering it and proposed taking the discs there.",["atomIDs"]={"2965:description:1-56","2965:description:59-142","2965:description:145-331","2965:description:336-449","2965:description:452-487","2965:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2965:completion:1-78","2965:completion:81-111","2965:completion:113-173","2965:completion:176-210","2965:completion:215-252","2965:completion:255-270","2965:completion:273-279","2965:completion:281-301","2965:completion:306-415"},["opening"]="Discussion of the recovered history reminded Truthseeker of Nara's travels. Her experience at the desert's Valley of the Watchers might connect the discs to the next inquiry.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to ask Nara about the valley.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Nara.",["sourceHash"]="d9aee4d2a2fd35abd40615d5f02396a7344a7a590af1f47c3d4f67c91010f7bd",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2966]={["aftermath"]="A watcher identified missing entry plates and instructed that they be added before another access attempt.",["atomIDs"]={"2966:description:1-105","2966:description:114-162","2966:description:167-211","2966:description:214-243","2966:description:246-290","2966:description:293-360","2966:description:363-423","2966:description:428-465","2966:description:467-495","2966:objective:1-124"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2966:completion:1-90","2966:completion:93-227","2966:completion:232-244","2966:completion:247-271","2966:completion:274-371","2966:completion:374-463","2966:completion:466-476"},["opening"]="Nara and the sage did not know whether the miniature records would act as keys or do nothing. The expedition to the sealed gates was an experiment in that uncertain connection.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the discs to Uldum's gates.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} activated the gate's clue with the discs.",["sourceHash"]="5a12af04d02e751208e3d183268371f411ba1c20a3a6d997901a90d93e3485ac",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2967]={["aftermath"]="Nara understood the records as part of a larger key set and weighed both promise and danger in opening the complex.",["atomIDs"]={"2967:description:1-93","2967:description:98-280","2967:objective:1-42"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2967:completion:1-28","2967:completion:31-163","2967:completion:168-258","2967:completion:261-329","2967:completion:334-463"},["opening"]="The discs were recovered from the pedestal after the watcher's instruction. Nara needed to hear what the gate lacked before the research could move further.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to report the missing plates.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the findings to Thunder Bluff.",["sourceHash"]="00918feb2cedeb4949e97444f8c6f1f555807af114b48621e168f0e9c69cd720",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2968]={["aftermath"]="Truthseeker agreed to wait for a narrower search area rather than pretend entry was already possible.",["atomIDs"]={"2968:description:1-10","2968:description:12-51","2968:description:54-138","2968:description:141-202","2968:description:205-343","2968:description:348-478","2968:objective:1-45"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2968:completion:1-138","2968:completion:140-263","2968:completion:268-417","2968:completion:419-455","2968:completion:457-488"},["opening"]="The needed plates were named, but their location remained unknown. Nara proposed research before another field journey and sent that conclusion to the sage.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to inform Truthseeker of the impasse.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Nara's conclusion.",["sourceHash"]="756a2f27af1edf48154371c9947bf92a8e77524fe760702e9a7b14e80aa4309d",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2969]={["aftermath"]="Kindal did not trust the darters' freedom to remain secure. She and Jer'kai prepared to move from rescue to an offensive against the captors.",["atomIDs"]={"2969:description:1-59","2969:description:61-158","2969:description:163-279","2969:description:284-431","2969:description:433-469","2969:description:471-495","2969:objective:1-86","2969:objective:88-148","2969:objective:153-238"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2969:completion:1-16","2969:completion:18-77","2969:completion:79-214","2969:completion:219-241","2969:completion:243-280","2969:completion:282-359","2969:completion:361-403"},["opening"]="Kindal and Jer'kai could not free the Grimtotems' captive faerie dragons alone. Kindal offered a cage key and her own help, but the rescue had to preserve her and at least six darters before a six-minute retreat.",["pending"]="{actor} would free the Sprite Darters and protect at least six of them and Kindal within the limit.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the timed rescue with at least six Sprite Darters and Kindal Moonweaver surviving.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b8075775f0827a5a4a612f70c19d35145e01bd6d3ae6c5ad17306e7b59b7a244",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2970]={["atomIDs"]={"2970:description:1-81","2970:description:83-232","2970:description:237-298","2970:description:300-368","2970:description:370-464","2970:objective:1-127"},["opening"]="Jer'kai and Kindal intended to carry the fight to the Grimtotem camps. Help against their naturalists, raiders and shaman could extend the retaliation beyond what the pair could accomplish alone.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to undertake the specified assignment against Grimtotem forces.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against twelve Naturalists, ten Raiders and six Shamans and returned to Jer'kai.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ce26148b57fca2386b05732955dc5b51dd226810ac67d2697a33e856d31228dd",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2972]={["aftermath"]="Tyrande accepted the account and intended to send Jer'kai's ring back with scouts heading for Feralas. The thanks carried another reason for the expedition to investigate.",["atomIDs"]={"2972:description:1-124","2972:description:126-145","2972:description:147-256","2972:description:258-315","2972:description:317-390","2972:description:395-416","2972:objective:1-78"},["bridge"]="The Grimtotem assignment had returned to Jer'kai. Her signet was to carry news of the two companions to Tyrande and lend weight to the account of the rescued dragons.",["bridgeFrom"]=2970,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2972:completion:1-28","2972:completion:30-117","2972:completion:119-154","2972:completion:156-258","2972:completion:260-334","2972:completion:339-407"},["opening"]="Jer'kai offered her signet as an introduction to Tyrande rather than a rich wilderness reward. In Darnassus, the ring would attest that the two companions were well and support the bearer's account.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take Jer'kai's Signet Ring to Tyrande.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Jer'kai's Signet Ring to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="47064b4ac93bb4993b973b22b6b1be191c5a55c5788f3dd874ac24111d0356c5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2973]={["atomIDs"]={"2973:description:1-13","2973:description:15-106","2973:description:111-251","2973:description:253-281","2973:description:283-349","2973:objective:1-79"},["opening"]="Krueg's mission for Orgrimmar left room for a gift to his life-mate. He wanted a cloak for Korrin ornamented with the shimmering wings of sprite darters west of Camp Mojache.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather ten Iridescent Sprite Darter Wings for Krueg.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Iridescent Sprite Darter Wings to Krueg Skullsplitter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ec9e9dc5695b946d625b54d1329b7a7ef648fe65a641d93cf85bba34dc8aada6",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2974]={["atomIDs"]={"2974:description:1-6","2974:description:8-42","2974:description:44-57","2974:description:59-83","2974:description:88-106","2974:description:108-130","2974:description:132-192","2974:description:194-224","2974:description:229-252","2974:description:254-288","2974:description:290-314","2974:description:316-374","2974:description:376-454","2974:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="News of Grimtotem tauren changed Krueg's attention from the cloak to Belgrom's bounty. He demanded horns as evidence while warning that the clan should not be underestimated.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover twenty Grimtotem Horns for Krueg.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twenty Grimtotem Horns to Krueg Skullsplitter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="7f5f70a2d1cf63353e13cf9b948ead1569d89167ebb26fa801d52a3b903bc582",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2975]={["atomIDs"]={"2975:description:1-76","2975:description:78-130","2975:description:132-199","2975:description:204-259","2975:description:261-287","2975:description:289-341","2975:objective:1-108"},["opening"]="Rok regarded the Gordunni outpost as a spreading scar on Feralas. The river north led to the ogres whose numbers he wanted reduced before their territory expanded further.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Rok's assignment against ten Ogres, ten Ogre-Magi and five Brutes.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Rok Orhan's assignment against the specified Gordunni groups.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="2bced290408064fdd5bafd9c4d01a3f6e6c3fab7f62840424b39494d04842bc2",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2976]={["aftermath"]="Belgrom regarded the Grimtotem sightings as news his peers would want. The horns supported a wider report as well as a bounty claim.",["atomIDs"]={"2976:description:1-6","2976:description:11-50","2976:description:52-101","2976:description:106-190","2976:description:192-245","2976:description:247-364","2976:description:369-428","2976:objective:1-68"},["bridge"]="The horns had reached Krueg, bringing his mention of Belgrom's bounty back to him. He crated the proof for delivery to Orgrimmar and the person responsible for paying it.",["bridgeFrom"]=2974,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2976:completion:1-15","2976:completion:17-36","2976:completion:38-91","2976:completion:93-98","2976:completion:103-143","2976:completion:145-202","2976:completion:207-305"},["opening"]="Krueg acknowledged that the bounty he had mentioned belonged with the person who did the work. The horns were crated for Belgrom in Orgrimmar, where the report and proof could be received.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to deliver the Crate of Grimtotem Horns to Belgrom.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Crate of Grimtotem Horns to Belgrom Rockmaul.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="65812e8d6ae3db321fb0362a3737e0d213f90ae3c42a2b4e72915f02a72ecf17",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2977]={["aftermath"]="Karnik understood the discs as only part of a set of keys. Finding the Plates might permit entry later, but the current discoveries did not provide them.",["atomIDs"]={"2977:description:1-93","2977:description:98-280","2977:objective:1-41"},["bridge"]="The Watcher's lesson had left entry dependent on the missing Plates of Uldum. The discs returned from the pedestal, ready to accompany the report back to Karnik.",["bridgeFrom"]=2954,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"2977:completion:1-28","2977:completion:31-163","2977:completion:168-258","2977:completion:261-361","2977:completion:366-412","2977:completion:414-426"},["opening"]="The pedestal had returned the discs, leaving the Watcher's lesson to carry home. Ironforge's researchers needed to hear what the desert visit had established.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to report the Uldum findings to Karnik.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Historian Karnik in Ironforge.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="9c669357209f6fc0382753bfe589733ef80586b4f4c22ade8470cc7347db10ed",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2978]={["atomIDs"]={"2978:description:1-104","2978:description:106-190","2978:objective:1-55"},["opening"]="A soiled Gordunni scroll depicted what might be a meeting or ceremony. Its meaning remained uncertain, but Rok Orhan had reason to examine the tribe's plans.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the Gordunni Scroll to Rok.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Gordunni Scroll to Rok Orhan.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3fd1034adfee6c2acc4832e6ca5bde06a6bfe7509192e273f7936bedb32191ee",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2979]={["aftermath"]="Rok planned to use the orb's information against the Gordunni. Obtaining it opened the investigation rather than explaining the ceremony outright.",["atomIDs"]={"2979:description:1-58","2979:description:60-137","2979:description:142-199","2979:description:204-332","2979:objective:1-59"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2979:completion:1-68","2979:completion:70-123"},["opening"]="Rok read the scroll as a dark ceremony conducted by Gordunni mage-lords. An orb from one of those mages could help reveal both the rite and the power behind it.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover a Gordunni Orb for Rok.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered a Gordunni Orb to Rok Orhan.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e8c42076d1ca3bfa8e9ded2ee8b5662c7b452f7011cd56680ef4bba1025675bf",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2980]={["atomIDs"]={"2980:description:1-125","2980:description:130-178","2980:description:180-276","2980:description:278-386","2980:description:388-402","2980:description:407-475","2980:description:477-485","2980:objective:1-109"},["opening"]="Rok sent the next effort into the High Wilderness, where ruined night elf structures and withered land marked the Gordunni presence. The shaman, warlocks and maulers there were stronger than the earlier outpost's foes.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake the assignment against ten Gordunni Shaman, ten Warlocks and five Maulers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Rok's High Wilderness assignment against the specified Gordunni forces.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="cfa19ca5b9a0070d1e37ba9f27d3723928c45839c511f67a86610b1f41531a05",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2981]={["atomIDs"]={"2981:description:1-80","2981:description:82-187","2981:description:189-254","2981:description:259-340","2981:description:342-397","2981:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Belgrom worried that the growing Gordunni force would endanger the Horde's Feralas presence. Rok at Mojache could provide the local account before another volunteer committed to the challenge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to meet Rok at Camp Mojache.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Belgrom's contact.",["sourceHash"]="468c51120a30629059ab94420a7f51d3499dbb9703606bf13ed1137055b99f91",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2982]={["atomIDs"]={"2982:description:1-107","2982:description:112-213","2982:description:215-325","2982:description:330-435","2982:description:437-507","2982:objective:1-99"},["opening"]="Angelas worried about Troyas entering the High Wilderness without her. Gordunni occupation made their shared study of Feralas' ruins dangerous, and she asked for the route made safer through an attack on the ogres.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to confront eight Gordunni Warlocks, eight Shaman and eight Brutes.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Angelas Moonbreeze's assignment against the three specified Gordunni groups.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3b761e33fb9aa7d61f8aba940039a1e86dfef18526f87183b6fd73dfd3c0dc05",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2983]={["atomIDs"]={"2983:description:1-51","2983:description:53-152","2983:description:154-184","2983:description:186-247","2983:description:252-287","2983:description:289-429","2983:objective:1-32"},["opening"]="Swart judged a shaman ready to face fire's power and its price. Kranal Fiss, living north of the Crossroads, was the teacher who could begin that trial.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to seek Kranal Fiss north of the Crossroads.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Kranal Fiss for instruction in fire.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="8472f547013794861ae0c9ffe4da8fac51eea00335d874a80ffe53874d6dd70e",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2984]={["atomIDs"]={"2984:description:1-48","2984:description:50-143","2984:description:145-199","2984:description:201-210","2984:description:212-296","2984:description:301-336","2984:description:338-466","2984:objective:1-32"},["opening"]="Narm Skychaser saw a new stage of shamanic study in fire, with destruction and chaos among its lessons. Kranal Fiss would test whether a pupil was prepared to pay the cost.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with Kranal Fiss north of the Crossroads.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Kranal Fiss to begin the fire instruction.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="768ff9b5ef6e2f222ac75a85dc3a33d440d27b732fb5ffb7fca85bbad5cf65fe",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2985]={["atomIDs"]={"2985:description:1-38","2985:description:40-120","2985:description:122-182","2985:description:187-226","2985:description:228-300","2985:description:302-344","2985:description:346-366","2985:objective:1-36"},["opening"]="Swart set a different test before a practiced shaman: the purity of water. Islen Waterseer waited on the eastern coast south of Ratchet, near a fishing hut.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to find Islen Waterseer on the coast south of Ratchet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Islen Waterseer for the water trial.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="2bb563cf3ca4054ebe447055f68577d98df93b839dc5cf26cbeff87a92c8b911",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2986]={["atomIDs"]={"2986:description:1-48","2986:description:50-143","2986:description:145-205","2986:description:210-249","2986:description:251-323","2986:description:325-367","2986:description:369-389","2986:objective:1-36"},["opening"]="Narm Skychaser regarded long study and patience as preparation for water's lessons. The next teacher, Islen Waterseer, lived along the eastern coast south of Ratchet.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Islen Waterseer by the coastal fishing hut.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Islen Waterseer to continue shamanic study.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="29a0009c5ef9a06f592abb06d25ae19d563b43f8fac012dfd3f9051e1ba035b4",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2987]={["atomIDs"]={"2987:description:1-130","2987:description:132-205","2987:description:207-318","2987:description:323-367","2987:description:369-444","2987:description:446-488","2987:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Orwin had heard of minerals the Gordunni buried to keep from outsiders. He offered a shovel and directed the search toward blue glows at the northern outpost, where twelve cobalt samples might be unearthed.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to dig up twelve Gordunni Cobalt samples for Orwin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twelve samples of Gordunni Cobalt to Orwin Gizzmick.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="217678eddd5af90225d60a8f32077ae82ebe92b585ab974627766dee74348953",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2988]={["aftermath"]="Sharpbeak was not found in those villages, leaving Talonaxe worried for the fleet's future.",["atomIDs"]={"2988:description:1-41","2988:description:43-173","2988:description:178-193","2988:description:196-278","2988:objective:1-88"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2988:completion:1-33","2988:completion:42-59","2988:completion:62-126","2988:completion:129-206"},["opening"]="Sharpbeak had vanished while hunting with his parents. Talonaxe feared for the young gryphon and suspected captivity in the Witherbark villages.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search both villages' cages.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the cage search to Talonaxe.",["sourceHash"]="46e7583269dad21a27e70fb96b44a624d45724db799bdead7cf51fe04c6ff83a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2989]={["aftermath"]="Talonaxe learned Sharpbeak was absent and found some relief that he had not been found at a place of sacrifice.",["atomIDs"]={"2989:description:1-45","2989:description:48-86","2989:description:89-188","2989:objective:1-74"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2989:completion:1-23","2989:completion:26-69","2989:completion:74-182","2989:completion:187-268"},["opening"]="The Witherbark search had failed, shifting suspicion to the Vilebranch. Talonaxe chose the Altar of Zul at the edge of their territory for the next inspection.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to search the altar's summit.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned with the altar search's findings.",["sourceHash"]="24dfe6e75283cb2c46622df004a4ca30dd079fe0fecbcc3cb91b192a6bd255b7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2990]={["aftermath"]="Thadius recognized a gryphon with a promising future, provided he survived undamaged.",["atomIDs"]={"2990:description:1-52","2990:description:55-153","2990:description:158-208","2990:description:213-280","2990:description:283-374","2990:description:379-392","2990:description:395-476","2990:objective:1-68"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2990:completion:1-8","2990:completion:11-49","2990:completion:52-83","2990:completion:85-127","2990:completion:132-152","2990:completion:155-184"},["opening"]="A feather from the missing gryphon's nest offered a link for divination. Talonaxe sent it to Thadius, a former Aerie Peak resident now pursuing darker knowledge at Nethergarde.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the feather to the diviner.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered it at Nethergarde.",["sourceHash"]="2a4d2fec1daf94e740a7cbddf4b17490a6affe7984c7fea881b9ef94219073cb",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2991]={["atomIDs"]={"2991:description:1-79","2991:description:82-188","2991:description:191-255","2991:description:260-328","2991:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Thadius offered to locate Sharpbeak only after another relic reached him. Nekrum Gutchewer's medallion in Zul'Farrak was the object he wanted to study in return for that help.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Nekrum's Medallion to Thadius.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Nekrum's Medallion to Thadius Grimshade.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="003e44fca7f79927721fd9c831e419d9b0ecadba378cc6bcd4aa91ec98668e12",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2992]={["aftermath"]="Thadius declared it successful and said he had seen Sharpbeak.",["atomIDs"]={"2992:description:1-52","2992:description:55-179","2992:description:184-193","2992:description:195-231","2992:description:234-256","2992:description:258-284","2992:objective:1-55"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2992:completion:1-25","2992:completion:28-82"},["opening"]="Thadius prepared to follow the connection between feather and owner. He warned that the ritual's success was conditional and asked for room to work.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to wait through the divination.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} remained for Thadius's ritual.",["sourceHash"]="a76dcab078ebe4bb3bbdec4122842b07b0414d528cd285290dca73916647bd27",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2993]={["aftermath"]="Talonaxe called for a rescue force once he learned the Vilebranch held the gryphon.",["atomIDs"]={"2993:description:1-90","2993:description:93-194","2993:description:199-204","2993:description:207-226","2993:description:229-264","2993:objective:1-35"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2993:completion:1-29","2993:completion:32-47","2993:completion:52-59","2993:completion:62-98","2993:completion:101-118","2993:completion:121-161"},["opening"]="The vision placed Sharpbeak in a cage atop Jintha'Alor. Thadius identified Hexx as the keyholder and sent the finding back to Aerie Peak.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to report the location to Talonaxe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} relayed the diviner's finding.",["sourceHash"]="502a7e305d75ca93649883bf0ad863c9c2d2a4a524956f7d09f2dde7cd7678d2",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2994]={["aftermath"]="The parents returned to Aerie Peak with their child, and Talonaxe welcomed the reunited family.",["atomIDs"]={"2994:description:1-23","2994:description:28-202","2994:objective:1-110"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2994:completion:1-104","2994:completion:107-190","2994:completion:195-248","2994:completion:251-338"},["opening"]="Talonaxe's rescue required a climb through the Vilebranch capital and the key taken from its high priestess. Sharpbeak's cage waited at the summit.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover the key and free Sharpbeak.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Sharpbeak's rescue.",["sourceHash"]="96b66b79ab09a282cabf7812d518c820bcd85475cf89c9e31415fdf66939fb5f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2995]={["aftermath"]="Oran expected the lost information to delay the elves while further barriers to their contacts were made.",["atomIDs"]={"2995:description:1-88","2995:description:90-276","2995:description:278-349","2995:description:354-415","2995:description:420-450","2995:description:453-499","2995:description:501-510","2995:objective:1-136"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"2995:completion:1-12","2995:completion:14-125"},["opening"]="Oran targeted the lodge's communication role and its efforts to form alliances. Records of shared knowledge about the Witherbark were to be burned rather than stolen for study.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to destroy the three Highvale document groups.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the destruction and reported to Oran.",["sourceHash"]="19e5562cdd68fcc7d53ede0c575c05cf8781aed8770f648f9bdd9a54e7b4ac9f",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2996]={["atomIDs"]={"2996:description:1-85","2996:description:87-128","2996:description:130-196","2996:description:198-240","2996:description:242-311","2996:description:313-326","2996:description:328-346","2996:description:348-385","2996:objective:1-35"},["opening"]="Gan'rul relayed a summons from Strahad Farsan. The human warlock's power made him a teacher worth seeking at the tower above Ratchet's port.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find Strahad Farsan at the tower overlooking Ratchet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} answered Strahad Farsan's summons in Ratchet.",["sourceClassMask"]="256",["sourceHash"]="fd7c50a45cd37740fdcbd9b4c909c0ef7f228a905dea14bfbb51259344593b74",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2997]={["atomIDs"]={"2997:description:1-10","2997:description:12-197","2997:description:199-312","2997:description:317-367","2997:description:369-420","2997:description:422-441","2997:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="Azar Stronghammer sent a paladin to learn further duties in service to the Light. Tiza Battleforge waited upstairs in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Tiza Battleforge in the Hall of Mysteries.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Tiza Battleforge for the next instruction.",["sourceClassMask"]="2",["sourceHash"]="5d882565361147a770d856391a7d73173f5898c624946aaeb96ec79115523bf5",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="4",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2998]={["atomIDs"]={"2998:description:1-29","2998:description:31-116","2998:description:118-193","2998:description:195-277","2998:description:282-354","2998:description:356-436","2998:objective:1-37"},["opening"]="Brother Wilhelm had heard favorable words about a paladin's progress. The next test lay with Duthorian Rall at Stormwind's cathedral.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek Duthorian Rall in the Cathedral of Light.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported to Duthorian Rall at the cathedral.",["sourceClassMask"]="2",["sourceHash"]="2a60b079e663cd1c64a16f7597a6bb0ba5be4a1001af88987a3009b4365b6d91",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="1",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[2999]={["atomIDs"]={"2999:description:1-10","2999:description:12-180","2999:description:182-295","2999:objective:1-38"},["opening"]="Brandur Ironhammer directed a paladin upstairs to Tiza Battleforge. The next lesson concerned duties owed to the Light rather than another exercise at the forge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Tiza Battleforge to receive the next instruction.",["sourceClassMask"]="2",["sourceHash"]="c09f6239caeaa019adeeac1fe10e1a075142a7771c1b5030e1dcb04e571eb30a",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="4",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3000]={["atomIDs"]={"3000:description:1-10","3000:description:12-203","3000:description:205-334","3000:description:339-425","3000:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sent a paladin back to the dwarven home of the order. Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge would explain the further duties of that calling.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to seek Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported to Tiza Battleforge for further paladin instruction.",["sourceClassMask"]="2",["sourceHash"]="188a42c388f9242fbf3eea1ee6dcc243f89e792fc0100764dd42df6764ec1d3a",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="4",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3001]={["aftermath"]="Strahad watched the port's labor with a warlock's contempt for its ignorance. He proposed turning his visitor's hostility to use.",["atomIDs"]={"3001:description:1-85","3001:description:87-128","3001:description:130-220","3001:description:222-238","3001:description:240-278","3001:description:280-361","3001:description:363-376","3001:description:381-410","3001:description:412-455","3001:objective:1-31"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"3001:completion:1-32","3001:completion:34-78","3001:completion:80-116","3001:completion:118-135","3001:completion:140-177","3001:completion:179-213"},["opening"]="Carendin Halgar had reached the limit of the lessons he offered. For greater summonings, he directed a pupil to Strahad in Ratchet, warning that the human's power deserved respect.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to seek Strahad Farsan beside the tower above Ratchet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.",["sourceClassMask"]="256",["sourceHash"]="2a5da12b60631c61eb5ed0a4a3e694e3edcc5fc03b6abc9a8c8dd7ea4ceaf4eb",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3002]={["aftermath"]="Uthel'nay recognized the orb as both powerful and dangerous. The response did not yet reveal the full nature of its magic.",["atomIDs"]={"3002:description:1-50","3002:description:52-106","3002:description:111-188","3002:description:190-204","3002:objective:1-72"},["bridge"]="The Gordunni Orb had reached Rok. Knowing his limits as a warrior, he sent it onward to Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar for the magical judgment it required.",["bridgeFrom"]=2979,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"3002:completion:1-18","3002:completion:23-73"},["opening"]="Rok knew the enemy as a warrior, but could not explain the orb's capabilities. Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar had the magical knowledge the Gordunni find required.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the Gordunni Orb to Uthel'nay.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Gordunni Orb to Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c25138d2cd4bb53180728916d01da3f5b3d4c5526c533629d49034cdafdc368e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3022]={["atomIDs"]={"3022:description:1-63","3022:description:65-108","3022:description:113-155","3022:description:157-259","3022:description:261-343","3022:objective:1-74"},["opening"]="Curgle entrusted a carefully packed crate of hippogryph eggs to a carrier for Rut'theran. Erelas Ambersky tended such eggs and trained the young creatures after hatching.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to deliver the Carefully-packed Crate to Erelas.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Carefully-packed Crate to Erelas Ambersky.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="bdaee93d87054f311e76a86e7aba00550807ec1cc5afa7fb10ce8632eae869c5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3042]={["atomIDs"]={"3042:description:1-132","3042:description:135-245","3042:description:250-286","3042:description:289-298","3042:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Trenton wanted the sandstone-derived tempering agent made by Zul'Farrak's Sandfury trolls. Connoisseurs prized the material he could use on his own crafted goods, and twenty vials would supply his work.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather twenty Vials of Troll Temper for Trenton.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twenty Vials of Troll Temper to Trenton Lighthammer.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3d43a90a4cfb50ad7de22038b9fd17aeb3de81140d751203e45f3bb15ecb2cf0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3062]={["aftermath"]="Talo accepted the heart as proof of Edana's death and planned to keep it as a remembrance of the deed.",["atomIDs"]={"3062:description:1-93","3062:description:95-158","3062:description:160-235","3062:description:237-289","3062:description:294-431","3062:description:436-506","3062:objective:1-66"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"3062:completion:1-36","3062:completion:38-102","3062:completion:104-113"},["opening"]="Talo named Edana Hatetalon as the Northspring queen and repeated reports of her crystalline heart. A horn sounded at the northern Hatetalon stones might summon her, giving access to the Dark Heart he demanded.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain Edana Hatetalon's Dark Heart for Talo.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Edana Hatetalon's Dark Heart to Talo Thornhoof.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="dcf950b5bd5c2ae42499421830a440f922d558a500c732b41fe11819d81cf050",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[3063]={["atomIDs"]={"3063:description:1-35","3063:description:37-83","3063:description:85-92","3063:description:97-183","3063:description:185-253","3063:description:258-306","3063:description:311-342","3063:description:344-417","3063:description:422-478","3063:description:480-498","3063:objective:1-138"},["opening"]="Talo's memory of a harpy ambush had survived long after his escape. Their cries still troubled the former hunter, and he asked for revenge against four kinds of Northspring harpy west of the camp.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to undertake Talo's four-part Northspring assignment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against four each of the Northspring Harpies, Roguefeathers, Windcallers and Slayers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3a034194a2fd32a7531fbe331d70c85c95acb2a7624ad9fb896a16d5fb9111ff",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
